<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Do I actually know this, or am I only confident about it?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If someone questioned me closely here, where would my account run out?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I treating skill in my own field as if it made me an authority on this question too?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I've only skimmed it, so I don't actually know. Here's what I'd need to check, and who has worked with them before?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "Yes, they're solid, I'm sure of it. Let's lock them in." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead is asked in a planning meeting whether a new supplier can deliver on time, and has only skimmed their proposal." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Separating what you know from what you merely feel sure of keeps a confident guess from becoming the team's decision, and invites the people who do know to speak." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Principle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Socratic ignorance" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Socrates' disavowal of knowledge" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Socratic wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "human wisdom" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "knowing that one does not know" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The teaching, drawn from Plato's Apology, that the beginning of human wisdom is not thinking you know what you do not know: an honest awareness of the limits of your own understanding, especially about the most important questions of how to live." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/foundations> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Socratic ignorance" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/know-thyself> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-method> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/wise-reasoning> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/socratic-ignorance/s1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/socratic-ignorance/s2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/socratic-ignorance> <http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/source/socratic-ignorance/s3> .
