<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask people who know this kind of decision, or only people who would agree with me?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Did I ask without signalling the answer I wanted?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "When the advice differed from my view, did I actually move, or did I explain it away?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I asked anyone who has already lived through this choice how it felt afterwards?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "I'll write down my own answer first, then ask a former colleague who joined a start-up two years ago how it really went, and a mentor who tends to be cautious. I won't tell them which way I'm leaning, and I'll actually shift my view if they both raise the same worry." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "I'll ask my best friend, who always backs me, mention the salary first, and take the yes as confirmation." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "A team lead has a job offer from a fast-growing start-up and must answer by Friday. They are excited and have already half-decided to accept." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Asking advisers who know the terrain, without steering them, gives the decision a second independent view and the lived experience of someone who has already been there, which people tend to undervalue." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1> <https://schema.org/position> "1"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1> <https://schema.org/text> "Name the decision and decide whether it is important and uncertain enough to deserve outside counsel." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2> <https://schema.org/position> "2"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2> <https://schema.org/text> "Write down your own current view and how confident you are, before you ask anyone." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3> <https://schema.org/position> "3"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3> <https://schema.org/text> "Choose two or three advisers who know this kind of situation, including at least one who has lived through it and one likely to disagree with you." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4> <https://schema.org/position> "4"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask each one separately and personally, describe the problem without revealing your preferred answer, and ask what they would do and why." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5> <https://schema.org/position> "5"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5> <https://schema.org/text> "Ask anyone who has already been through the same choice how it actually turned out and felt for them." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6> <https://schema.org/position> "6"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6> <https://schema.org/text> "Compare their answers with your own and move your view meaningfully toward the advice where they know more or agree with each other, noting where and why you still differ." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowToStep> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7> <https://schema.org/position> "7"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7> <https://schema.org/text> "Make the decision yourself, take responsibility for it, and later tell your advisers what you decided and how it went." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://schema.org/HowTo> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/name> "Seeking counsel" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/1> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/2> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/3> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/4> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/5> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/6> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto> <https://schema.org/step> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel/howto/7> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-12"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Practice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Seeking counsel" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "advice seeking" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "asking for advice" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "taking counsel" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "wise counsel" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/deliberation> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "Deliberately asking well-chosen people for their view before an important or uncertain decision, and then giving their advice real weight rather than only using it to confirm what you already think." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/judgment-and-decisions> .
