<https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox#graph> {
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "If a friend brought me this exact problem, what would I tell them, and am I following that advice myself?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Could I state the other person's view in words they would accept as fair?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Have I admitted what I don't know about their motives and about how this could unfold?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#SelfCheckQuestion> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Am I treating any compromise as a defeat?" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/check/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Rewrite> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#after> "If my teammate described this to me, I'd ask what they actually know about the peer's reasons, what a fair split could look like, and how it might look in a month. I'll ask the peer for ten minutes first." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#before> "This is a power grab, plain and simple. I know exactly what they're up to, and I'm escalating to our director today." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#situation> "You recently helped a teammate think calmly through a clash with another department. This week a peer quietly reassigns part of your own project without asking you." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox/example> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#why> "Treating your own conflict as you would a colleague's brings back the habits you already use as an adviser, namely admitting what you don't know, looking for compromise and expecting the situation to change." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-11-13"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/ontology#Obstacle> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Solomon's paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "Solomon paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel> "self-other asymmetry in wise reasoning" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/egocentric-bias> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition> "The tendency to reason more wisely about other people's problems than about our own: people facing a friend's conflict more readily admit what they do not know, seek compromise, weigh other viewpoints and expect change than they do when the same conflict is theirs." .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/scheme/science-of-wisdom> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel> "Solomon's paradox" .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/giving-advice> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/intellectual-humility> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/interpersonal-conflict> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/perspective-taking> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/seeking-counsel> .
  <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/solomons-paradox> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related> <https://github.com/john1hsu/wisdom-graph/id/self-distancing> .
